{"TopicsController#unsubscribe dereferences tu.notification_level and tu.save! even when TopicUser.find_by returns nil or when notification_level is NULL, causing a 500 error instead of toggling state": 0.9900482892990112, "The unsubscribe action is protected by ensure_logged_in, so logged-out users clicking from email cannot unsubscribe, defeating the primary email-driven unsubscribe path": 0.9385454058647156, "The unsubscribe action modifies TopicUser.notification_level and calls save! but is routed via HTTP GET, bypassing Rails CSRF protection and allowing attackers to forge unsubscribe requests via embedded img tags or link prefetching": 0.9421989321708679, "When context_posts are present, the notification email template contains %{respond_instructions} both inside the conditional block and unconditionally at the bottom, causing the respond instructions text to appear twice in the rendered email": 0.9097179174423218}